From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] Settings: no grey bands

Measured on V86 (2026-10-27) by counting the grey levels of each region of a
screenshot rather than of a whole page. The first count was of whole pages and
was wrong twice over: it put the Files application's illustration down as that
application's chrome, which is white, and it missed that the main Settings
page is already white.

  | region                                             | grey | pixels  |
  |----------------------------------------------------|------|---------|
  | sub-page title bar (storage, about, apps, network) |  245 | ~106000 |
  | storage page, the band under the title bar         |  238 |  239300 |

Rule 1 of docs/design/eink-ui.md names #F5F5F5 and #EEEEEE as colours that land
on panel level 14, one level from white, and so cannot mark a region. Both
reach Settings from the framework through the theme: the title bar is
?attr/colorPrimary, primary_device_default_light, primary_material_light,
material_grey_100; and the band is ?attr/colorSecondary,
secondary_device_default_settings_light, secondary_material_settings_light,
material_grey_200.

They are changed here and not in the framework because rule 3 asks for the
page's own white with a black rule of 1dp (2 px), and a rule needs a drawable.
Adding one to framework-res would add a resource name, which moves every
resource ID after it, and with them framework.jar and the ART boot image; an
application may add names freely. Settings is also the only place the greys
were measured. Quick settings is white but for 7,573 px of level 14, recents
is white, the Files application is white, and the main Settings page already
draws its own white search card (patch 0004).

The drawable reuses the outline colour and width that patch 0004 put in
res/values/pw3_eink.xml, so the two are defined once.

--- a/res/values/themes.xml
+++ b/res/values/themes.xml
@@ -211,6 +211,9 @@
 
     <style name="Theme.ActionBar" parent="@android:style/Widget.Material.ActionBar.Solid">
         <item name="android:contentInsetStart">@dimen/actionbar_contentInsetStart</item>
+        <!-- PW3: white with the rule that marks its lower edge, in place of
+             Material's grey 100 (docs/design/eink-ui.md rules 1 and 3). -->
+        <item name="android:background">@drawable/pw3_bottom_rule</item>
     </style>
 
     <style name="Theme.ActionBar.SubSettings" parent="Theme.ActionBar">
--- a/res/layout/storage_summary_donut.xml
+++ b/res/layout/storage_summary_donut.xml
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 <LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
     android:layout_width="match_parent"
     android:layout_height="wrap_content"
-    android:background="?android:attr/colorSecondary"
+    android:background="@drawable/pw3_bottom_rule"
     android:gravity="center_vertical"
     android:orientation="horizontal" >
 
--- /dev/null
+++ b/res/drawable/pw3_bottom_rule.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
+<!-- PW3: a band of the page's own white, with the rule that marks its lower
+     edge (docs/design/eink-ui.md). Material sets such a band apart with a grey
+     one panel level from white, which rule 1 names as a colour that cannot mark
+     a region here; rule 3 marks it with the outline instead. The values are the
+     ones Settings already carries in res/values/pw3_eink.xml. -->
+<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
+    <item>
+        <shape android:shape="rectangle">
+            <solid android:color="@color/pw3_outline" />
+        </shape>
+    </item>
+    <item android:bottom="@dimen/pw3_outline_width">
+        <shape android:shape="rectangle">
+            <solid android:color="?android:attr/colorBackground" />
+        </shape>
+    </item>
+</layer-list>
